      {
        "id": "urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.840cafe72b485226a010e3a70b81bb6ef16159ab.001.1",
        "event": "Special Weather Statement",
        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued August 25 at 1:10PM AKDT by NWS Fairbanks AK",
        "description": "Areas of rain on Tuesday will transition to snow in the Eastern\nBrooks Range Tuesday evening. Snow then continues through the day\non Wednesday. Given the rain beforehand, snow will struggle to\naccumulate immediately but there will be minor accumulations by\nWednesday morning. Wednesday afternoon there may be a brief break,\nallowing snow to gradually melt. Then snow returns Wednesday\nevening before diminishing into snow showers Thursday morning.\n\nSnow totals around 1 to 2 inches are expected overn",
        "severity": "Moderate",
        "certainty": "Observed",
        "urgency": "Expected",
